## Investigation Report: i18n for `plugins/pantoken/layouts`

I've completed a thorough exploration of the layouts plugin and the i18n infrastructure elsewhere in the repo. Here's what I found:

---

### 1. **Layouts Plugin Structure**

[plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/layouts/](plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/layouts/) contains:

- **Page layouts** (simple HTML compositions):
  - [pages/page-layout.ts](plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/layouts/pages/page-layout.ts) — type definition with `name`, `title`, `html`, `imagePlaceholders`
  - 10 layout files: [about-me.ts](plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/layouts/pages/about-me.ts), [hero.ts](plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/layouts/pages/hero.ts), [course-home.ts](plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/layouts/pages/course-home.ts), [footer.ts](plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/layouts/pages/footer.ts), [header.ts](plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/layouts/pages/header.ts), [callout.ts](plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/layouts/pages/callout.ts), [rubric-note.ts](plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/layouts/pages/rubric-note.ts), [syllabus.ts](plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/layouts/pages/syllabus.ts), [testimonial.ts](plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/layouts/pages/testimonial.ts), [two-column.ts](plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/layouts/pages/two-column.ts)
  - [pages/index.ts](plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/layouts/pages/index.ts) exports `pageLayouts: readonly PageLayout[]` (sorted by title)

**Example hardcoded strings** (from [about-me.ts](plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/layouts/pages/about-me.ts)):
```ts
export const aboutMe: PageLayout = {
  name: "about-me",
  title: "About me",  // ← English label
  html: `<h1 class="instui-heading">About your instructor</h1>
    <p class="instui-text">Share a brief introduction...</p>
    <h2 class="instui-heading">How to reach me</h2>
    ...`,  // ← English prose/headings
  imagePlaceholders: [{
    key: "instructor-photo",
    altText: "A photo of the instructor",  // ← English alt text
  }]
};
```

**Downstream consumers:**
- [renderers/tinymce/src/layouts.ts](renderers/tinymce/src/layouts.ts) — re-exports `pageLayouts`, `PageLayout` from `@pantoken/plugin-layouts`
- [renderers/tinymce/src/plugins/layouts.ts](renderers/tinymce/src/plugins/layouts.ts#L78) — `createLayoutsPlugin` accepts layouts and renders them (optionally resolving image placeholders)
- Canvas theme editor template imports `@pantoken/plugin-layouts/layouts.css` and passes layouts config to `createPantokenPlugin()`
- All referenced in `packages/pantoken` meta-package and docs API generation

---

### 2. **How i18n Works Elsewhere for CLI/Scaffold Packages**

**Pattern: Messages-kind space with i18n.json source → generated locale bundles**

**i18n.config.json** ([root](i18n.config.json)):
```json
{
  "spaces": {
    "cli.scaffold": {
      "kind": "messages",
      "source": "packages/scaffold/src/i18n.json"
    },
    "ui.strings": {
      "kind": "messages",
      "source": "renderers/web-components/src/i18n.json"
    },
    "cli.ai": {
      "kind": "messages",
      "source": "ai/pantoken-ai/src/i18n.json"
    }
  }
}
```

**Source file structure** ([packages/scaffold/src/i18n.json](packages/scaffold/src/i18n.json) excerpt):
```json
{
  "promptPlatform": {
    "message": "Select a platform to scaffold:",
    "translate": "always"
  },
  "promptDir": {
    "message": "Target directory:",
    "translate": "always"
  },
  "spinnerStart": {
    "message": "Scaffolding...",
    "translate": "always"
  }
}
```

**Runtime lookup pattern** ([packages/scaffold/src/locale.ts](packages/scaffold/src/locale.ts#L120)):
```ts
export function createLocaleLookup(
  bundles: Record<string, Record<string, string>>,
  resolvedLocale: string,
  fallback = "en",
): LocaleLookup {
  const resolved = bundles[resolvedLocale] ?? bundles[fallback] ?? {};
  const fallbackBundle = bundles[fallback] ?? {};
  return {
    locale: resolvedLocale,
    t: (key: string, params?: Record<string, string>) => {
      const msg = resolved[key] ?? fallbackBundle[key] ?? key;
      // Substitute {{param}} placeholders
      return params ? msg.replace(/\{\{(\w+)\}\}/g, (_, k) => params[k] ?? "") : msg;
    }
  };
}
```

**At build time** ([packages/scaffold/scripts/generate.ts](packages/scaffold/scripts/generate.ts)):
- Loads `i18n.json` + all scaffold template `scaffold.json` (nextSteps/notes/caveats) + template `src/i18n.json`
- Calls `generateMessageBundles()` from `@pantoken/i18n-engine` (part of `tools/i18n-engine/`)
- Generates `packages/scaffold/generated/locales/index.ts` (exports `MESSAGES: Record<locale, Record<key, string>>`)
- Generates `packages/scaffold/generated/locale-registry.ts` (maps locale tags to text directions)

**CLI consumption** ([packages/scaffold/src/cli.ts](packages/scaffold/src/cli.ts)):
```ts
const locale = detectLocale({ langFlag: options.lang });
const lookup = createLocaleLookup(MESSAGES, locale);
const message = lookup.t("promptPlatform"); // "Select a platform to scaffold:"
```

---

### 3. **Dependencies & i18n Infrastructure in Repo**

**Tools:**
- `@pantoken/i18n-engine` ([tools/i18n-engine/](tools/i18n-engine/)) — core extraction, gettext (PO/POT), drift checking, translation pipeline
- `@pantoken/translation-adapters` ([tools/translation-adapters/](tools/translation-adapters/)) — shared markdown masking, docs/i18n translation CLI facade

**Layouts plugin package.json** ([plugins/pantoken/layouts/package.json](plugins/pantoken/layouts/package.json)):
- Currently has no i18n dependency
- Depends on: `@pantoken/model`, `@pantoken/plugin-kit`

**Existing partial i18n in layouts** ([plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/lib/](plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/lib/)):
- [slot-labels.ts](plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/lib/slot-labels.ts) — skeleton for i18n lookup (`slotLabel()`, `slotLabelsByLocale()`, `registerSlotLabels()`)
- [extract-slot-placeholders.ts](plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/lib/extract-slot-placeholders.ts) — extracts strings from `:slot()` pseudo-element CSS rules
- These are **not yet integrated** with the main i18n pipeline — marked as placeholders for "a full implementation"

---

### 4. **Documentation & Known Gotchas**

**Build/docs conventions** ([docs/conventions/build-and-docs.md](docs/conventions/build-and-docs.md)):
- The `vp` toolchain is mandatory; package scripts must never shell out to `pnpm` (CI has no pnpm, only `vp`)
- Generated artifacts (including locale bundles) are gitignored and reproduced on every build
- `pnpm run ready` is the build gate (parallel tasks: build → check/test/lint concurrently)
- Docs site has three builds for different locales (English-only for CI, all locales for deploy)

**i18n gotchas** ([/memories/repo/i18n-translation-gotchas.md]()):
- `DOCS_TRANSLATION_TIMEOUT_MS` env must be set on direct `node scripts/...` calls, not `vp run`
- Translation batches can silently fail if they exceed timeouts; grep for `^\s*!` in logs to find real failures
- Drift checks differ by surface: `docs:check:drift` is separate from generic `i18n check <namespace>` CLI

**Tests** ([plugins/pantoken/layouts/tests/](plugins/pantoken/layouts/tests/)):
- [index.test.ts](plugins/pantoken/layouts/tests/index.test.ts) — plugin capability/CSS structure tests
- [layouts/layout-templates.test.ts](plugins/pantoken/layouts/tests/layouts/layout-templates.test.ts) — (exists but not read; structure matches other test patterns)

---

### 5. **Summary: Pattern for Adding i18n to Layouts**

**Recommended approach** (follows existing scaffold pattern):

1. **Create** `plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/i18n.json` — source map of all hardcoded strings:
   ```json
   {
     "aboutMe.title": { "message": "About me", "translate": "always" },
     "aboutMe.heading1": { "message": "About your instructor", "translate": "always" },
     "aboutMe.paragraph1": { "message": "Share a brief introduction...", "translate": "always" },
     // ... all ~50 strings across 10 layouts + alt text
   }
   ```

2. **Update** `i18n.config.json` to add a new space:
   ```json
   {
     "spaces": {
       "layouts.strings": {
         "kind": "messages",
         "source": "plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/i18n.json"
       }
     }
   }
   ```

3. **Generate** locale bundles via a build script (`plugins/pantoken/layouts/scripts/generate.ts`), similar to scaffold's pattern:
   - Call `generateMessageBundles()` from `@pantoken/i18n-engine`
   - Output to `plugins/pantoken/layouts/generated/locales/index.ts` (exports `MESSAGES`)

4. **Create** lookup helper (`plugins/pantoken/layouts/src/lib/i18n.ts`):
   ```ts
   import { createLocaleLookup, type LocaleLookup } from "@pantoken/scaffold";
   import { MESSAGES } from "../generated/locales/index.ts";

   export function createLayoutsLocale(locale: string): LocaleLookup {
     return createLocaleLookup(MESSAGES, locale);
   }
   ```

5. **Refactor** `PageLayout` type to accept `locale` parameter or use a factory pattern:
   - Option A: `getPageLayouts(locale: string): PageLayout[]` — returns layouts with translated strings
   - Option B: Keep `PageLayout` immutable, provide a translation wrapper at consumption time (less invasive)

6. **Update tests** — ensure translated/fallback strings are tested

7. **Update downstream** (`renderers/tinymce`, templates, docs) — pass locale when requesting layouts

**Key advantage:** Reuses existing `@pantoken/i18n-engine` infrastructure, integrates with repo's drift checking and translation pipeline; new namespace `layouts.strings` flows through same `i18n` CLI, PO/POT generation, and locale-specific JSON rendering.
